# Draft: winemac: Send mouse input directly and add rawinput from GCMouse.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11999 state=opened
# I was thinking we could now do something like that prior to !11799, to avoid queuing the mouse input messages twice, and benefit directly from the win32u mouse motion accumulation support. However I can't seem to get GCMouse do anything on my local setup for some reason and I can't really tell if it's working or not. Sending mouse input directly does seem to work though, it should only involve a wineserver call and no user messages (hooks are triggered and waited directly from wineserver for non-injected input).
